{
  "description": "Swipe to confirm: motion (9.34.0, «x-swipeConfirmMotion», «Button.confirmTransition»). Refines 9.22 and 9.24, whose tables stay as they are. Numbers are logical points from the inline START of the button; times are milliseconds. The pattern is the Flutter package swipeable_button_view: the fill follows the thumb, the button collapses into a circle with the busy indicator (600 ms, fastOutSlowIn = cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)), and with «ripple» the circle grows over the whole screen (800 ms, linear), then the action runs and the next screen shows from under the fill (200 ms, linear). Curve values were computed independently (bisection, 80 steps); compare to 1e-4.",
  "labelCases": [
    {
      "name": "at rest the label is fully seen",
      "progress": 0,
      "expect": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "half the travel — half seen",
      "progress": 0.5,
      "expect": 0.5
    },
    {
      "name": "at the threshold",
      "progress": 0.9,
      "expect": 0.1
    },
    {
      "name": "at the end the label is gone",
      "progress": 1,
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "past the end — clamped",
      "progress": 1.4,
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "below zero — clamped",
      "progress": -0.2,
      "expect": 1
    }
  ],
